From c6b9426bc2d45133d4ffa02e50b3d593584fd761 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:52:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/53] B70-IP-PAD16: QSA views, fused writer and int8-dot
 gathers (K6/K7/K8) follow the 16-B padded per-token-head slot

1. qsa_pth_kv_views splits at the cache's half (content // 2) and validates it
   with pth_check_half instead of asserting C == 2 * (D + 4).
2. qsa_prepare (fused writer) takes the head dim from the QK-norm width and
   writes V at MAIN_V_OFF = content // 2 (new constexpr) instead of D + 4; pad
   bytes are never written.
3. attn2 ALIGN8 (B70_QSA_I8DOT): i8dot_align_kwargs decides ALIGN8 plus
   KV_ALIGN (16 when cell, strides and V offset are 16-B multiples, as with
   the padded 544-B cell; 8 for the tight 520-B cell) and V_OFF (the V offset
   in bytes); the kernel addresses V as K + V_OFF. i8dot_align8 stays as the
   bool. The warmup uses the same kwargs from the real views.

Tests (CPU, Triton interpreter; every test runs on the padded and the tight
layout): spec 544/520, views vs TRITON_ATTN and no byte written, wrong content
refused, writer -> attn2 / split-K round trip (rel < 1e-2 vs dequant ref),
fused writer bytes == writer formula with pads untouched, unfused update,
int8-dot kernels, ALIGN8 V_OFF 272 / KV_ALIGN 16 on the padded cell.
